BISON brain tissue segmentation library and command line
Copyright 2026 Neurodesk contributors

This package ports the BISON (https://github.com/VANDAlab/BISON, 94dd5f8) and
BISON-WMH (https://github.com/VANDAlab/BISON-WMH, ee973df) pipelines by Mahsa
Dadar and D. Louis Collins.

The model files (models/ in a release, or the download cache) are listed with
their licences in model.manifest.json:
- The BISON classifiers, priors and histograms: the BISON licence, a BSD-style
  licence that requires its notice, in models/LICENCE-BISON.txt.
- The BISON-WMH classifier, priors, histograms and average FLAIR: redistributed
  with the permission of Mahsa Dadar (2026-10-24); BISON-WMH's CITATION.cff
  names Apache-2.0.
- The ICBM 2009c nonlinear symmetric template and mask: Copyright (C) 1993-2009
  Louis Collins, McConnell Brain Imaging Centre, Montreal Neurological
  Institute, McGill University. Use and redistribution are permitted with the
  notice in templates/COPYING.

Registration and denoising run in WebAssembly: greedy-rs (exes/greedy, Apache-2.0,
a port of Greedy by Paul Yushkevich), antsRegistration and DenoiseImage from
ANTs (Apache-2.0, ANTsX contributors) with ITK (Apache-2.0), and niimath
(BSD-2-Clause, Chris Rorden). The classifiers run on ONNX Runtime (MIT).

Dadar M, Collins DL (2021). BISON: Brain tissue segmentation pipeline using T1-
weighted magnetic resonance images and a random forest classifier. Magn Reson
Med 85(4):1881-1894.
Dadar M, Maranzano J, Misquitta K, et al. (2017). Performance comparison of 10
different classification techniques in segmenting white matter hyperintensities
in aging. NeuroImage 157:233-249.
